IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g5-interpretation`
IMPORT `g5-nouns`
IMPORT `g5-art13-effects`
IMPORT `g5-art13-reporting`
IMPORT `g5-art14-court-powers`
IMPORT `g5-tests-fixtures`

-- g5-tests-forks.l4: for each fork of group G5 (F5.1 to F5.13), the discriminating case of the register in FRAGMENT-G5.md, run under each reading.
-- The expected value under each reading was decided from the text of the reading (the words that license it), not from the code.
-- The record `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14` has one field per fork; `the favoured interpretation` takes the reading marked "taken".

§ `Tests of the forks of Articles 13 and 14`

`the favoured reading` MEANS `the favoured interpretation of Articles 13 and 14`

§§ `F5.1 -- "promptly" (Article 13(6)); F5.10 -- counting the days`

-- Case 1 (reading B against reading C).  A matter arose on 1 March 2026; the charity became aware of it on 20 March 2026; it reported on 25 March 2026;
-- 14 days are allowed.  Counted from the event the last prompt day is 15 March, so the report is late; counted from awareness it is 3 April, so it is in time.
`the March matter` MEANS `Timing of a matter under Article 13(6)` WITH
    `date of the event or proposal` IS YMD 2026 3 1
    `date the charity became aware of the matter` IS YMD 2026 3 20

`a report on 25 March 2026, judged not prompt` MEANS `Report of a matter under Article 13(6)` WITH
    `date the report was made` IS JUST (YMD 2026 3 25)
    `the report was made promptly` IS FALSE

`a report on 10 March 2026, judged not prompt` MEANS `Report of a matter under Article 13(6)` WITH
    `date the report was made` IS JUST (YMD 2026 3 10)
    `the report was made promptly` IS FALSE

#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(6) the report was made promptly` (`the interpretation with promptness measured from the event in` 14) `the March matter` `a report on 25 March 2026, judged not prompt`
#ASSERT `Art 13(6) the report was made promptly` (`the interpretation with promptness measured from awareness in` 14) `the March matter` `a report on 25 March 2026, judged not prompt`
-- Case 2 (reading A against reading B).  A report on 10 March that the reader judges not prompt: on reading A it is not prompt (the input says so); on reading B it is within 14 days of the event.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(6) the report was made promptly` `the favoured reading` `the March matter` `a report on 10 March 2026, judged not prompt`
#ASSERT `Art 13(6) the report was made promptly` (`the interpretation with promptness measured from the event in` 14) `the March matter` `a report on 10 March 2026, judged not prompt`
-- F5.10, when "promptly" is 14 days from the event: reading A (taken) counts 15 March as the last prompt day, reading B (the day of the event is day one) 14 March.
`a report on 15 March 2026, judged not prompt` MEANS `Report of a matter under Article 13(6)` WITH
    `date the report was made` IS JUST (YMD 2026 3 15)
    `the report was made promptly` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 13(6) the report was made promptly` (`the interpretation with promptness measured from the event in` 14) `the March matter` `a report on 15 March 2026, judged not prompt`
#ASSERT `F5.10 A: the last prompt day when the day of the event is not counted` (YMD 2026 3 1) 14 EQUALS YMD 2026 3 15
#ASSERT `F5.10 B: the last prompt day when the day of the event is the first day` (YMD 2026 3 1) 14 EQUALS YMD 2026 3 14

§§ `F5.2 -- the year to which the return relates (Article 13(7), 13(9)(a)); F5.11 -- an anniversary on 29 February`

-- A payment to a governor on 10 February 2026 by the Arts Trust (registered 1 March 2019), financial year ending 30 June.
`the financial year end of 30 June` MEANS JUST (`Day on which a financial year ends` OF 6, 30)

`a day in the autumn of 2026` MEANS YMD 2026 12 1
`a day in the spring of 2026` MEANS YMD 2026 3 15

`a payment on 10 February 2026` MEANS `Payment to a governor or a connected person` WITH
    description IS "a consultancy fee of 12,000 pounds"
    `date of the payment` IS YMD 2026 2 10
    `made by or on behalf of the registered charity` IS TRUE
    `made to a governor of the charity` IS TRUE
    `made to a person having a prescribed connection with a governor` IS FALSE
    `of a description prescribed by the Order` IS TRUE
    `the annual return gives its details` IS FALSE

-- For the return covering 1 December 2026: calendar year 2026 (A) holds 10 February 2026; financial year 2026-27 (B) does not; the year from the anniversary of registration, 1 March 2026 to 28 February 2027 (C), does not.
#ASSERT `Art 13(9)(a) the payment falls within the year to which the return relates` `a payment on 10 February 2026` (`Art 13(7) the year to which the return relates` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` NOTHING `a day in the autumn of 2026`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(9)(a) the payment falls within the year to which the return relates` `a payment on 10 February 2026` (`Art 13(7) the year to which the return relates` `the interpretation with the charity's own financial year` `the Arts Trust` `the financial year end of 30 June` `a day in the autumn of 2026`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(9)(a) the payment falls within the year to which the return relates` `a payment on 10 February 2026` (`Art 13(7) the year to which the return relates` `the interpretation with the year from each anniversary of registration` `the Arts Trust` NOTHING `a day in the autumn of 2026`)
-- For the return covering 15 March 2026: A (calendar 2026) and B (1 July 2025 to 30 June 2026) hold the payment; C (1 March 2026 to 28 February 2027) does not.
#ASSERT `Art 13(9)(a) the payment falls within the year to which the return relates` `a payment on 10 February 2026` (`Art 13(7) the year to which the return relates` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` NOTHING `a day in the spring of 2026`)
#ASSERT `Art 13(9)(a) the payment falls within the year to which the return relates` `a payment on 10 February 2026` (`Art 13(7) the year to which the return relates` `the interpretation with the charity's own financial year` `the Arts Trust` `the financial year end of 30 June` `a day in the spring of 2026`)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(9)(a) the payment falls within the year to which the return relates` `a payment on 10 February 2026` (`Art 13(7) the year to which the return relates` `the interpretation with the year from each anniversary of registration` `the Arts Trust` NOTHING `a day in the spring of 2026`)
-- F5.11.  A charity registered on 29 February 2020; the reference day 28 February 2025; the year of the return being the twelve months from each
-- anniversary of registration (reading C of F5.2).  Reading A (taken): the anniversary in 2025 is 28 February, so the year containing 28 February 2025
-- began on 28 February 2025.  Reading B: the anniversary is 1 March 2025, so 28 February 2025 ends the year that began on 29 February 2024.
#ASSERT `Art 13(7) the year to which the return relates` `the interpretation with the year from each anniversary of registration` `the leap day charity` NOTHING (YMD 2025 2 28) EQUALS `Year to which an annual return relates` OF (YMD 2025 2 28), (YMD 2026 2 27)
#ASSERT `Art 13(7) the year to which the return relates` `the interpretation with the year from each anniversary of registration and 29 February rolled` `the leap day charity` NOTHING (YMD 2025 2 28) EQUALS `Year to which an annual return relates` OF (YMD 2024 2 29), (YMD 2025 2 28)

§§ `F5.3 -- "any Order under paragraph (7), (8) or (9)" (Article 13(10))`

#ASSERT `Art 13(10) the relief Order names the provision` `the favoured reading` `a provision of an Order under paragraph (8)` `a provision of an Order under paragraph (7) made by virtue of paragraph (8)`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(10) the relief Order names the provision` `the interpretation with no Order under paragraph (8)` `a provision of an Order under paragraph (8)` `a provision of an Order under paragraph (7) made by virtue of paragraph (8)`

§§ `F5.4 -- "misconduct in the administration of the charity" (Article 14(1)(a))`

`a conviction with no bearing on the administration` MEANS `What appears to the court under Article 14(1)` WITH
    `the conduct concerns the administration of the charity` IS FALSE
    `the conduct is misconduct in the ordinary sense` IS FALSE
    `it is necessary or desirable to exercise the power to protect the charity's property or secure its proper application` IS FALSE

`mismanagement that breaks no provision` MEANS `What appears to the court under Article 14(1)` WITH
    `the conduct concerns the administration of the charity` IS TRUE
    `the conduct is misconduct in the ordinary sense` IS TRUE
    `it is necessary or desirable to exercise the power to protect the charity's property or secure its proper application` IS FALSE

-- Case 1: misconduct within Article 2(10) with no bearing on the administration: A no, B yes, C no.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(1)(a) there is or has been misconduct in the administration of the charity` `the favoured reading` TRUE `a conviction with no bearing on the administration`
#ASSERT `Art 14(1)(a) there is or has been misconduct in the administration of the charity` `the interpretation with any misconduct` TRUE `a conviction with no bearing on the administration`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(1)(a) there is or has been misconduct in the administration of the charity` `the interpretation with misconduct in the ordinary sense` TRUE `a conviction with no bearing on the administration`
-- Case 2: mismanagement in the administration that is not misconduct within Article 2(10): A no, B no, C yes.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(1)(a) there is or has been misconduct in the administration of the charity` `the favoured reading` FALSE `mismanagement that breaks no provision`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(1)(a) there is or has been misconduct in the administration of the charity` `the interpretation with any misconduct` FALSE `mismanagement that breaks no provision`
#ASSERT `Art 14(1)(a) there is or has been misconduct in the administration of the charity` `the interpretation with misconduct in the ordinary sense` FALSE `mismanagement that breaks no provision`

§§ `F5.5 -- is a return sent on the due date timely? (Article 13(8))`

`an Order due on 31 March 2027` MEANS `Order under Article 13(7) and (8)` WITH
    `due date of the annual return` IS JUST (YMD 2027 3 31)
    `consequence of lateness` IS NOTHING

#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(8) the annual return is late` `the favoured reading` `an Order due on 31 March 2027` (YMD 2027 3 31)
#ASSERT `Art 13(8) the annual return is late` `the interpretation with a return due before the due date` `an Order due on 31 March 2027` (YMD 2027 3 31)

§§ `F5.6 -- the day deregistration takes effect (Article 13(1))`

#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(1) paragraphs (2) to (4) apply on the day` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust, deregistered with effect from 30 June 2022` (YMD 2022 6 30)
#ASSERT `Art 13(1) paragraphs (2) to (4) apply on the day` `the interpretation with the effective day inside the registration` `the Arts Trust, deregistered with effect from 30 June 2022` (YMD 2022 6 30)

§§ `F5.7 -- "a purpose that is not charitable" (Article 13(2))`

`the Arts Trust day` MEANS YMD 2023 1 1
#ASSERT `Art 13(2) the provision of the constitution is of no effect` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` `the Arts Trust day` `a provision permitting a purely ancillary purpose`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(2) the provision of the constitution is of no effect` `the interpretation with ancillary purposes not caught` `the Arts Trust` `the Arts Trust day` `a provision permitting a purely ancillary purpose`

§§ `F5.8 -- paragraphs (a) and (b) of Article 13(5)`

#ASSERT `Art 13(5) the registered charity in the restricted section meets what paragraph (5) requires` `the favoured reading` `a charity with a prior permission that still meets its original condition and fails the different one`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(5) the registered charity in the restricted section meets what paragraph (5) requires` `the interpretation with the permission replacing the condition` `a charity with a prior permission that still meets its original condition and fails the different one`

§§ `F5.9 -- the first day of a period fixed by the court (Article 14(3)(a), (b), (g))`

`a hold for 30 days from 1 June 2026` MEANS `a specified period` (YMD 2026 6 1) 30
#ASSERT `Art 14(3) the order is in operation on the day` `the favoured reading` `a hold for 30 days from 1 June 2026` (YMD 2026 6 1)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(3) the order is in operation on the day` `the interpretation with the court period starting the day after` `a hold for 30 days from 1 June 2026` (YMD 2026 6 1)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(3) the order is in operation on the day` `the favoured reading` `a hold for 30 days from 1 June 2026` (YMD 2026 7 1)
#ASSERT `Art 14(3) the order is in operation on the day` `the interpretation with the court period starting the day after` `a hold for 30 days from 1 June 2026` (YMD 2026 7 1)

§§ `F5.12 -- the three purposes of an order under Article 14(2)`

`an order only to protect the property` MEANS `Order that the court sees fit under Article 14(2)` WITH `to remedy the misconduct` IS FALSE, `to protect the property` IS TRUE, `to secure its proper application` IS FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 14(2) the order is one the court sees fit` `the favoured reading` `an order only to protect the property`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 14(2) the order is one the court sees fit` `the interpretation with all three purposes` `an order only to protect the property`

§§ `F5.13 -- when a matter "arises" for the annual return (Article 13(7))`

`an event of 30 December 2026 that the charity learned of on 5 January 2027` MEANS `Timing of a matter under Article 13(6)` WITH
    `date of the event or proposal` IS YMD 2026 12 30
    `date the charity became aware of the matter` IS YMD 2027 1 5

`the calendar year 2026` MEANS `Year to which an annual return relates` OF (YMD 2026 1 1), (YMD 2026 12 31)

#ASSERT `Art 13(7) the matter arose during the year to which the return relates` `the favoured reading` `the calendar year 2026` `an event of 30 December 2026 that the charity learned of on 5 January 2027`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(7) the matter arose during the year to which the return relates` `the interpretation with the date of awareness` `the calendar year 2026` `an event of 30 December 2026 that the charity learned of on 5 January 2027`

§§ `F5.14 -- which statement a payment is judged by (Article 13(11)(a))`

-- The first statement (10 January 2022) is contradicted by the payment of 10 May 2023; the amended statement (1 February 2023) is not.
-- Reading A (taken): the statement in force is the amended one, so the payment is consistent.  Reading B: "a statement provided" includes the first.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(11)(a) the payment is inconsistent with the statement` `the favoured reading` `a payment that fits the amended statement but not the first`
#ASSERT `Art 13(11)(a) the payment is inconsistent with the statement` `the interpretation with any statement provided` `a payment that fits the amended statement but not the first`

